@* Radix aligns its panel with the chosen item so the current value stays under the pointer. The
   OS decides that here, and each platform decides differently — macOS overlays the value, Windows
   drops below. It cannot be configured, and matching one of them would be wrong on the other. *@
<Field Class="w-[280px]">
    <FieldLabel For="sa-size">Size</FieldLabel>
    <Select id="sa-size" name="size">
        <SelectItem Value="xs">XS</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="s">S</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="m" Selected>M</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="l">L</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="xl">XL</SelectItem>
    </Select>
    <FieldDescription>Open it: where the panel lands is the operating system's decision.</FieldDescription>
</Field>
